in @reality
in @bauchladen
in @uuid/spectral

# @reality/algebra — the species-root for altitude-specific
# matter+information realizations under @reality.
#
# A prism that imports `in @reality/algebra` declares its content IS
# one species under the @reality family-root — one altitude at which
# the substrate's 5-op gauge action operates uniformly across
# matter-aspect and information-aspect carriers per `reality.md` §2.2.
#
# Per `reality.md` §3.1 the path-namespace discipline:
#
#   `shards/reality.mirror`               declares `@reality` family-
#                                          root and ONLY that.
#   `shards/reality/algebra.mirror`       declares `@reality/algebra`
#     (THIS SHARD)                         species-root and ONLY that;
#                                          the sub-prism class one
#                                          altitude under @reality.
#   `shards/reality/algebra/<alt>.mirror` declares one species per
#                                          altitude and ONLY that.
#
# This shard lands the SPECIES-ROOT level — the typed namespace that
# all six species shards specialize. Without it, species shards' `in
# @reality/algebra` resolves to nothing. Per the Taut Pass-2 scout
# ordering finding, the species-root MUST land before any species
# shard; this tick discharges that ordering by landing the family-
# root, species-root, and the math species in dependency order.
#
# === The species pattern ===
#
# Per `reality.md` §3.3 the species pattern is uniform across all
# `@reality/algebra/<altitude>` shards. Each species declares four
# constituents per the canonical spec:
#
#   1. **matter_carrier** — the matter-side type carrier for this
#      altitude. By gauge-collapse semantics this is a NOMINAL label,
#      not a distinct type. The label conveys to human-facing readers
#      that this aspect of the orbit is the matter-side.
#
#   2. **information_carrier** — the information-side type carrier
#      for this altitude. By gauge-collapse semantics this is the
#      SAME TYPE as matter_carrier, with a different label. The
#      label conveys the information aspect.
#
#   3. **gauge_action** — the 5-op algebra at this altitude. The
#      altitude-specific parameterization of the substrate's 5-op
#      block. The only altitude-specific variation is the H_altitude
#      space on which the algebra acts.
#
#   4. **witness_predicate** — the substrate-decl predicate verifying
#      the four invariances of `reality.md` §2.5 (algebra closure,
#      Hilbert linearity, Dirac equivariance, spectral action
#      invariance) at the species altitude. Dischargeable at the
#      empirical altitude (LAPACK for silicon, Mesland operations
#      for spectral, etc.).
#
# Under gauge-collapse (path-c uniformity per `reality.md` §2.3),
# matter_carrier and information_carrier ARE THE SAME TYPE at each
# altitude. They are two labels for the same underlying H_altitude
# state. The shard declaration shape (substrate-decl, illustrative;
# the canonical per-altitude version lands in
# `shards/reality/algebra/<altitude>.mirror`):
#
#   prism @reality/algebra/<altitude> <= @reality/algebra {
#     type matter_carrier      = H_<altitude>
#     type information_carrier = H_<altitude>
#     witness algebra_closure     <- closure_under_5op_at_<altitude>
#     witness hilbert_linearity   <- linearity_under_5op_at_<altitude>
#     witness dirac_equivariance  <- equivariance_under_kintsugi_at_<altitude>
#     witness spectral_invariance <- action_invariance_under_glue_at_<altitude>
#     focus <altitude>
#     project <altitude>
#     split <altitude>
#     shift <altitude>
#     settle <altitude>
#   }
#
#   out @reality/algebra/<altitude>
#
# === The species inheritance chain ===
#
# Per `reality.md` §3.1 the inheritance chain is:
#
#   @autopoietic
#     ↑                            (fold-back permission)
#   @reality                       (family-root; gauge-action
#     ↑                             uniformity; #106 candidate)
#   @reality/algebra               (species-root; typed namespace;
#     ↑                             THIS SHARD)
#   @reality/algebra/<altitude>    (per-altitude species; per-altitude
#                                   matter+information realization)
#
# Each level adds discipline:
#   - @autopoietic adds fold-back permission.
#   - @reality adds gauge-action uniformity + the gauge_orbit carrier.
#   - @reality/algebra (this shard) adds the species_descriptor carrier
#     + the typed namespace under which per-altitude species live.
#   - @reality/algebra/<altitude> adds the altitude-specific
#     (matter_carrier, information_carrier) labels + the
#     altitude-specific witness predicates.
#
# === The six species (forward-promised; math lands this tick) ===
#
# Per `reality.md` §3.2 the substrate has been pulling on six species
# at various altitudes:
#
#   silicon   hardware-altitude (subsumes today's @silicon at
#             `27e9067`); matter aspect = transistor state; info
#             aspect = executable algebra-of-silicon.
#   nl        natural-language altitude (lifts @nl + @metalogue);
#             matter aspect = waveform/bytes; info aspect =
#             proposition/meaning. Autopoietic recursion: every nl
#             crystal becomes input to future nl emissions.
#   code      code altitude (lifts @facet/<lang> + @cascade); matter
#             aspect = source text; info aspect = denotational
#             semantics.
#   physics   physical-reality altitude (cosmos-mirror's territory);
#             matter aspect = field configuration; info aspect =
#             gauge structure / Lagrangian. Settlement at 2D/3D has
#             a DEGENERATE form (Forman-Ricci fragments); species
#             shard MUST declare fragmentation as valid crystal state.
#   spectral  spectral altitude (the substrate operating on its own
#             spectral triples per #100); matter aspect = (A, H, D)
#             object; info aspect = representation theory + Mesland
#             correspondences. Species shard MUST inherit `in @glue`
#             rather than re-declare Tomm probes (already a @glue
#             species per `shards/glue.mirror`).
#   math      math altitude (LANDS THIS TICK); matter aspect = formal
#             mathematical object; info aspect = mathematical content
#             the object encodes. Per `805676e`: the highest-
#             reflexive species; A IS the content. Discharge to
#             LaTeX/Lean/Coq/Agda/Mathematica via @io.
#
# Each species MUST declare its @io discharge target(s); the species-
# root names this as obligation through the io_discharge_declared
# predicate inherited from @reality.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Path-namespace classes  the substrate's path-namespace pattern
#                           per [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-
#                           source]]; consistent application of the
#                           `<path>.mirror declares @<path>` rule.
#   Species-roots           consistent precedent in `shards/algebra/
#                           metalogue.mirror` (sub-prism under
#                           `@algebra`); `shards/spectral/metalogue.
#                           mirror` (sub-prism under `@spectral`); the
#                           pattern is uniform across the substrate.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/reality.md §3.1 (path-namespace
#               discipline); §3.3 (species pattern: four constituents);
#               §8.1 (substrate-decl shard forward-promises naming
#               this shard explicitly: "the species root declaration
#               . Declares `@reality/algebra` and ONLY that. Inherits
#               `<= @reality`. Path-namespace declaration:
#               `shards/reality/algebra.mirror` declares the sub-prism
#               class one altitude under @reality.");
#               docs/specs/reality-algebra-math-and-glue.md §1.1
#               (the math species' specialization of this species-
#               root's pattern; the illustrative shard code shows
#               `prism @reality/algebra/math <= @reality/algebra { ... }`
#               which requires this species-root to resolve).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-connes-spectral-triple]],
#                      [[architecture-mirror-as-expanding-hilbert-space]] (#51),
#                      [[architecture-at-x-is-mathematical-value]]
#                       (@reality/algebra at value position is the
#                        species-root ref; admissible at value
#                        positions in species shards),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (species_descriptor
#                        is a typed carrier; no bare altitude string),
#                      [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] (no operational
#                        species this tick except math; species follow
#                        when consumers pull),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (the species-root pattern was implicit in
#                        the canonical spec; this shard makes it
#                        addressable as a substrate-decl object).
# Related shards: reality.mirror (the family-root this shard
#                  inherits from; the gauge_orbit carrier consumer
#                  species shards observe at their altitudes),
#                 reality/algebra/math.mirror (the first species
#                  landing this tick; the highest-reflexive of the
#                  six per `805676e`),
#                 bauchladen.mirror (the content-addressing discipline
#                  species crystals respect),
#                 algebra.mirror (the substrate's algebra family-root;
#                  the A side of the Connes spectral triple species
#                  shards' gauge actions operate within; sibling
#                  family-root at the top-level path-namespace, not
#                  parent of this shard).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/reality/algebra.mirror`
# declares `@reality/algebra` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/math/connes-1985
source @arxiv/math/connes-1995-reality

prism @reality/algebra <= @reality {
  # Species-root for altitude-specific matter+information
  # realizations under @reality. The typed namespace under which
  # `@reality/algebra/<altitude>` species shards live.
  #
  # Per `reality.md` §3.3 each species declares four constituents:
  # matter_carrier, information_carrier, gauge_action,
  # witness_predicate. By gauge-collapse semantics (path-c
  # uniformity per `reality.md` §2.3) matter_carrier and
  # information_carrier are the SAME TYPE at each altitude — two
  # nominal labels on the same H_altitude state.
  #
  # The species-root's 5-op block operates over species_descriptor
  # (the typed handle for "one altitude under @reality/algebra/*");
  # per-altitude shards specialize the 5-op block to their
  # H_altitude carrier.
  focus species_descriptor
  project species_descriptor
  split species_descriptor
  shift species_descriptor
  settle species_descriptor
}

# === The species_descriptor carrier ===
#
# A typed record per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming one species
# under `@reality/algebra/*`. Lifts the per-altitude declaration shape
# from `reality.md` §3.3 into a typed carrier the species-root level
# can reference.
#
# - `altitude`            the substrate-ref naming the altitude the
#                         species sits at; one of {silicon, nl, code,
#                         physics, spectral, math, ...}. Must match
#                         the species shard's path-namespace
#                         declaration per `@epistemologic/pact/path_
#                         matches_namespace`.
# - `matter_label`        the species-specific human-facing label
#                         for the matter aspect (e.g., "transistor
#                         state" for silicon, "utterance" for nl,
#                         "mathematical object" for math); nominal
#                         per `reality.md` §3.3.
# - `information_label`   the species-specific human-facing label
#                         for the information aspect (e.g.,
#                         "executable algebra" for silicon,
#                         "proposition" for nl, "mathematical
#                         content" for math); nominal per §3.3.
# - `io_discharge_target` the ref naming the species' @io discharge
#                         target(s); MUST be declared per the
#                         `io_discharge_declared` obligation
#                         inherited from @reality. Examples:
#                         `@io/silicon` (cargo/LLVM/LAPACK);
#                         `@io/nl` (conversational/paper);
#                         `@io/math` (LaTeX/Lean/Coq/Agda).
# - `witness_predicate`   the species-altitude four-invariances
#                         witness predicate ref; the discharge
#                         carrier per `reality.md` §3.3 item 4.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (altitude,
# io_discharge_target). Two species_descriptor records ARE the
# same species under content-addressing iff both the altitude ref
# and the io_discharge_target ref are byte-equal. The labels are
# nominal; the witness_predicate is the discharge mechanism, not
# the identity.
type species_descriptor = {
  altitude:            ref,
  matter_label:        ref,
  information_label:   ref,
  io_discharge_target: ref,
  witness_predicate:   ref,
}

# === enumerate_orbits — list all gauge_orbits at this species ===
#
# Given a species_descriptor, returns the list of gauge_orbits
# (from @reality.gauge_orbit) currently registered at the species'
# altitude. The list is the species' current Bauchladen content
# at @reality altitude — the prior-art crystals @fate consults
# when the next species inference fires.
#
# Body discharges per-species at the realisation boundary.
enumerate_orbits(s: species_descriptor) -> [gauge_orbit] { \ }

# === species_witnessing inheritance predicate ===
#
# `species_witnessing(s)` is the predicate consumer shards name in a
# `requires` clause to declare bilateral commitment (per recognition
# #37, the Pask-agreement reading of `requires`) that the
# species_descriptor `s` IS a valid `@reality/algebra/*` species —
# i.e., the species declares all four constituents per `reality.md`
# §3.3 (matter_label, information_label, io_discharge_target,
# witness_predicate) AND the species' io_discharge_target satisfies
# `io_discharge_declared(s.altitude)` inherited from @reality.
#
# Sibling to:
#   - `reality.reality_witnessing(o)` (the gauge-orbit inheritance
#     predicate this shard's per-orbit registrations transitively
#     discharge through the species' witness_predicate).
#   - `bauchladen.bauchladen_witnessing(crystal)` (the crystal-
#     altitude inheritance predicate species' orbit-crystals honor).
#
# Forward-promised inheritors:
#
#   - `@reality/algebra/math` (THIS TICK): the math-altitude species
#     per `805676e`; the highest-reflexive species (A IS the content).
#   - `@reality/algebra/silicon` (forward-promised): subsumes today's
#     @silicon work at `27e9067`.
#   - `@reality/algebra/nl` (forward-promised): lifts @nl + @metalogue.
#   - `@reality/algebra/code` (forward-promised): lifts @facet/<lang>
#     + @cascade.
#   - `@reality/algebra/physics` (forward-promised): cosmos-mirror's
#     territory; MUST declare fragmentation as valid crystal state.
#   - `@reality/algebra/spectral` (forward-promised): MUST inherit
#     `in @glue` and read @spectral/metalogue as morphism family.
#
# No `requires species_witnessing(...)` clauses at THIS shard. The
# species-root declares the predicate; consumers add the clauses
# when they pull.
species_witnessing(s: species_descriptor) -> verdict { \ }

out @reality/algebra
out species_descriptor
out enumerate_orbits
out species_witnessing
